title: HaroldAudenLibrary
---
Harold Auden: Harold pulls a dusty book off the shelf. Looking at the cover, he discovers some unusual runes engraved into it. He runs his fingers across them before opening the book to the first page. 
->Title: “A History of the Vikings”
    <<add_fear "Harold Auden">>
    <<discover_fear "Harold Auden" 3>>
    <<terrified "Harold Auden">>
    //Fear of Violence
    Reading past the first page, he is taken aback by the brutal illustrations of people’s bodies being torn apart. One particular illustration of the Blood Eagle, a ritualistic torture method, lingers in his mind even after he puts the book away. 
->Title: “The New England Journal of Medicine”
    <<neutral "Harold Auden">>
	He skims past a couple of diagrams before putting the book back on the shelf. 
->The text is unintelligible. 
    <<neutral "Harold Auden">>
	“Strange.” He puts the book back where he found it. 
-> Title: “Different Seasons”
    <<reduce_fear "Harold Auden">>
    <<determined "Harold Auden">>
    A smile spreads wide across  his face. He loved this book in high school. He carries it under his coat, hoping it will keep him company through his long journey. 
===

title: HaroldAudenDungeon
---
Harold Auden: Harold feels uneasy as he steps into the room. He looks down at his feet to find them soaking in a  pool of blood. He jumps away, putting him face-to-face with the contents of one of the cells.
->It’s an old man sulking in the corner.
    <<neutral "Harold Auden">>
	Confused, he bangs on the bars of the cell. The figure looks up, makes brief eye contact with Harold, and then fades into air. 
->It’s a mound of flesh.
    <<add_fear "Harold Auden">>
    <<discover_fear "Harold Auden" 7>>
    <<terrified "Harold Auden">>
    //Fear of the Inhuman
    Something about this scene feels familiar to him. The mound of flesh begins to move to reveal two eyes staring at him, hanging off long nerves. He screams but can’t take his eyes off of it as it fades into air.  
->Nothing is there.
    <<neutral "Harold Auden">>
	“Huh. I could’ve sworn I saw something.” He continues on. 
->It’s a rabid dog.
    <<neutral "Harold Auden">>
	“Hi, doggy.” Harold is comforted by the bars that separate him from the mutt. The dog snarls before fading into air.  
===

title: HaroldAudenDiningRoom
---
Harold Auden: As Harold enters the dining room, he feels a shiver run up his spine.
->”Wonder why it’s so cold…”
    <<neutral "Harold Auden">>
    Harold wonders what the frigid temperature in the room might mean about where he is.
->”It must be a ghost.”
    <<neutral "Harold Auden">>
	“A ghost?” He considers the implications of this potential reality, but he can’t think of a logical reason to be scared.
->”That’s not the cold. Something is running up your spine.”
    <<add_fear "Harold Auden">>
    <<discover_fear "Harold Auden" 6>>
    <<terrified "Harold Auden">>
    //Fear of Parasites
    He grabs at his back but can’t seem to reach his spine. He feels like something is crawling under his skin. He collapses to the floor and shakes with terror. 
->”Must be the wind.”
    <<neutral "Harold Auden">>
    “Yeah, that must be it.” Harold continues on.
===

title: HaroldAudenCemetery
---
Harold Auden: The strange patch of grass at the center of this labyrinth perplexes Harold. He walks past the gravestones, reading the names on each one. He comes across one headstone that beckons him closer. It reads… 
->Jay Telzrow, 1913 - 1987, Beloved Mayor
    <<neutral "Harold Auden">>
  	“Seems perfectly normal.” Harold continues on his way.
->Gray Huff, 1924 - 1996, Dedicated Dentist
    <<neutral "Harold Auden">>
	“Weird to put the word dentist on your headstone.” Harold continues on his way. 
->Franklin Auden, 1942 - 2012, Loving Father
    <<add_fear "Harold Auden">>
    <<discover_fear "Harold Auden" 5>>
    <<terrified "Harold Auden">>
    //Fear of Parents
    “Dad!?” Shocked to be  reminded of his father in this place, he hears his dad’s voice in his mind. He glances at the grave plot next to his father’s and sees his mother’s eyes staring up at him through the grass. Even in death, they watch him. They judge him.
->Alex Lacoste, 1950-2003, Forgotten
    <<neutral "Harold Auden">>
	“What does that mean?” Puzzled, he stares at the gravestone.
===

title: HaroldAudenRitualRoom
---
Harold Auden: Something overtakes Harold as he enters the room. He starts shaking and can barely keep his balance. He looks at the lectern holding a book with cryptic runes.
->”Like a church.”
    <<add_fear "Harold Auden">>
    <<discover_fear "Harold Auden" 1>>
    <<terrified "Harold Auden">>
    //Religious Trauma
    A memory takes hold of him. He sees his mother scolding him in the pews of a huge church hall, and a tall pastor stares menacingly at him. The thought of those eyes following him makes him feel weak, helpless.  
->”What do those runes read?”
    <<neutral "Harold Auden">>
	He looks closer, inspecting it thoroughly. He can’t find a satisfying answer.
->”What is this room used for?”
    <<neutral "Harold Auden">>
	He can’t figure it out. The book suggests some sort of ritual was performed here. 
->”Look at these nice candles!”
    <<neutral "Harold Auden">>
	“Wow. Those are nice!”

===

title: HaroldAudenBedroom
---
Harold Auden: Harold looks at the bed. It reminds him of the days he spent locked in his room as a child, forced to watch through the window at other kids as they played.
->”You were so sick all the time.”
    <<neutral "Harold Auden">>
    “Yeah, I was. Mother was always so worried about me.” Harold explores the room.
->”Remember how the neighborhood kids used to treat you?”
    <<add_fear "Harold Auden">>
    <<discover_fear "Harold Auden" 4>>
    <<terrified "Harold Auden">>
    //Fear of Being Ridiculed 
	A memory rushes back to him. The kids threw rocks at his window, taking bets on who could break the glass and hit him in the head. He swears he can hear their faint laughter.  
->”You’re an adult now. Grow up.”
    <<neutral "Harold Auden">>
	“Yeah, I should grow up.” Harold continues on.
->”Mom used to come and take care of you.”
    <<neutral "Harold Auden">>
    “Yeah. Mother was always so worried about me.” Although those memories hold mixed emotions, it wasn’t all bad. Harold explores the room.
===

